*  CONTROL FOR CLASS (a), AND A THIRD CLASS IN ITS OWN RIGHT -- NO FENCE ANYWHERE.  body_root IS
*  published (no RESUME-NIL line) and the blob is STILL red: an ALT top whose arm is itself a concat
*  ending in an alternation publishes the arm's first node as the resume carrier, so an external
*  beta re-enters an exhausted inner alternation and concedes instead of walking out to the ALT.
*  Not the fence rung; own row.  The barer twin ( 'a' | 'aa' ) is green, which is what makes this
*  a carrier-SELECTION defect and not a missing-carrier one.
          P = ( 'a' ('b' | epsilon) | 'aa' )
          'aa' POS(0) *P RPOS(0)                :S(OK)F(NO)
OK        OUTPUT = 'match'                      :(END)
NO        OUTPUT = 'nomatch'
END
